<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/ecosystem> dcterms:title "Harm to an Ecosystem" ;
	linkml:description "Harm that falls on interconnected systems and resources." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/end_users> dcterms:title "End users" ;
	skos:altLabel "End Users" , "End-Users" ;
	linkml:description "The people or groups who use the system, whether new to technology or expert in AI." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/environment> dcterms:title "The environment" ;
	linkml:description "The natural environment." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/explainable_and_interpretable> dcterms:title "Explainable and Interpretable" ;
	linkml:description "Its working can be represented (how a decision was made) and its output understood in context (why, and what it means for the user)." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/fair_with_harmful_bias_managed> dcterms:title "Fair – with Harmful Bias Managed" ;
	linkml:description "Addresses equality and equity, including harmful bias and discrimination, knowing that views of fairness differ across cultures and applications." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/financial_or_supply_systems> dcterms:title "Global financial system, supply chain, or interrelated systems" ;
	linkml:description "To large systems that link organizations." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/float> a linkml:TypeDefinition ;
	skos:editorialNote "If you are authoring schemas in LinkML YAML, the type is referenced with the lower case \"float\"." ;
	skos:exactMatch "schema:Float"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/linkml/types"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:base "float" ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/linkml/Float"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "A real number that conforms to the xsd:float specification" ;
	linkml:imported_from "linkml:types" ;
	linkml:uri "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/general_public> dcterms:title "General public" ;
	linkml:description "Those most likely to experience the impacts directly, who may motivate what other AI actors do." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/governance_and_oversight> dcterms:title "Governance and Oversight" ;
	linkml:description "Holding management, fiduciary and legal authority for the organization where the system is designed, developed or deployed." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/group_or_community> dcterms:title "Group/Community" ;
	linkml:description "To a group, such as discrimination against a sub-group of a population." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/groups> dcterms:title "Groups" ;
	linkml:description "Groups of people." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/human_baseline> dcterms:title "Human baseline" ;
	linkml:description "A system that augments or replaces human activity needs a baseline, which is hard to systematize." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/human_cognitive> dcterms:title "Human-cognitive" ;
	linkml:description "In how people perceive system information to decide, or think about what a system is for." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/human_factors> dcterms:title "Human Factors" ;
	linkml:description "Human-centered design and evaluation, involving end users and bringing context-specific norms and values into design." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/individual> dcterms:title "Individual" ;
	linkml:description "To a person's civil liberties, rights, safety or economic opportunity." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/individuals> dcterms:title "Individuals" ;
	linkml:description "Particular people." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/informing> dcterms:title "Informing audience" ;
	linkml:description "AI actors in the People and Planet dimension, who inform the primary audience." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/inscrutability> dcterms:title "Inscrutability" ;
	linkml:description "Opaque systems, poor documentation and inherent uncertainty complicate measurement." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-100-1/integer> a linkml:TypeDefinition ;
	skos:editorialNote "If you are authoring schemas in LinkML YAML, the type is referenced with the lower case \"integer\"." ;
